# These three must keep Windows line endings, whatever git would prefer.
#
# `cmd.exe` mis-parses a batch file with Unix endings — every line is read
# wrong, and `REM` arrives as an unknown command called `M`. That bug was found
# and fixed by hand, and then git announced it would put it straight back on
# the next checkout: "CRLF will be replaced by LF the next time Git touches it".
#
# `.reg` is the same story: the registry importer wants CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.reg text eol=crlf
